<title>HONG KONG: China Everbright up after asset purchase.</title>
<headline>China Everbright up after asset purchase.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of China Everbright-IHD Pacific Ltd rose after an announcement that its parent would inject assets into the company, brokers said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Anticipation of more asset injection in future following the deal, resulting in a rise in asset value, fueled buying,&quot; said a senior sales manager at a regional brokerage.</p>
<p>Its shares rose HK$0.50 or 9.71 percent to HK$5.65 in mid-morning on volume of 15.67 million shares.</p>
<p>China Everbright-IHD said it had finalised the purchase of a 20 percent stake in International Bank of Asia Ltd and a 2.5 percent stake in National Mutual Asia Ltd from its parent for a total of HK$1.14 billion.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (952) 2843 6370</p>
